  "figure_review": [
    "Exact requested X-axis wording is retained, with signed error change on X and molecular weight on Y. Positive=worse is correct in the formula and verification manifest, but not explained by the axis text alone; put the formula and negative=better/positive=worse once in an adjacent caption or report text, without altering the literal axis label.",
    "Shared padded limits, square panels, a restrained zero reference, single-color direct points, no regression lines, and explicit stratum counts support honest comparisons. Full sets and stratified panels preserve all rows.",
    "The four charge/potency facets expose overlap limitations, but the absent small net-neutral higher-potency subgroup is implicit; retain an explicit zero-count coverage table in the sidecar/report. Current strata CSV omits that empty cell rather than miscounting it.",
    "Tiny translucent points may obscure density and the rare two-compound small/higher-potency subgroup; use the coverage table for interpretation, not apparent point density. Do not crop MW extremes without disclosing omitted points.",
    "Rendered generator in memory using its original plotting body and a read-only save callback; only its final manifest-write AST statement was suppressed in memory. Verified axes, plotted totals, point limits and visible text canvas bounds. No exported image or browser visual inspection was performed; host save callback styling remains outside this review."
  ],
